   "bodyText": "<p paraeid=\"{0edba5a9-2899-446d-b88a-052605c9a763}{252}\" paraid=\"783098417\">Cape Taputapu offers the best illustration in American Samoa of wave action on older massive volcanic activity which created Tutuila Island.  </p> <p paraeid=\"{bc63d6b0-e0ab-45fc-928a-a6faae96d25d}{5}\" paraid=\"1278649821\">Directions: Drive the coast road west to the village of ‘Amanave. Park off the road just before the road makes a sharp right turn uphill. The cape is about a mile walk along the shoreline. ONLY HIKE AT LOW TIDE. </p>",
