   "bodyText": " It was completed in 1917. This was a particularly important facility because it was the only U.S. Naval station established south of the equator. The radio station helped maintain communications with places throughout the South Pacific, including New Zealand, Australia, and British, German, and French possessions in the region. The facility was renovated again in 1970, and the original radio tower was removed. Today, the building serves a completely different purpose. It is now used as the Territorial Registrar’s Office.",
