   "latLong": "-14.27871789297339,-170.68885628386028",
   "bodyText": "This open area is Malae-ole-Talu, which served as the ceremonial center and parade grounds of the Naval station. The space continues to have an important community function today as the parade grounds used by the village of Fagatogo. After the signing of the deed of session, this open area was used for flag day celebrations, until 1980, when the last Flag Day parade was held at Malae-ole-Talu following the tragic plane crash that destroyed the Rainmaker Hotel. ",
